ver  everything in fact you know I definitely  won't be able to go over everything go  so I'll be talking for days but I would  also like to highlight kilowatt  immediately because his journey is the  exact opposite of God's kilowatt starts  a series in a place of darkness having  been raised as an assassin but by this  point his empathy and passion shines  brighter than anything else in this arc  and in my opinion kilowatt becomes the  emotional core of everything outside of  Kaimuki that is and it's tragic in its  own way to follow this boy who really  the only thing he wants to do in this  world is protect his best friend and to  see him have to go to such extreme  lengths in order to achieve that kill  Allah is betrayed is almost entirely  selfless and is a perfect counterbalance  to go on in this arc and the series as a  whole Plus this is also the arc that  highlights his fantastic known abilities  in God speed in particular is such a  great development for him and one of my  favorite Alec moments would be where he  implemented it against you P and this  Hawk has so many more stars on the  traditional side of the protagonist but  I do need to step back a bit now and  talk about the ants because going into  this I never would have thought that I  would be capable of feeling for such  beings I was so incredibly worried that  marijuana in particular would just turn  out to be an overpowered cell knock off  but he actually turned out to be in my  opinion one of the best written  characters in the series if not  literature as a whole and I know that  every other youtubers talked about this  to death but Mara when really is the  perfect example of how to implement an  overpowered villain at no stage during  the sock was marijuana event on the cusp  of needing to get serious so much so  that he didn't even really create any  net abilities he came naturally equipped  with one  to being or synthesis and he absorbs  some abilities from his royal guard but  this guy was 