ind a powerful opponent  which he did and I have to say that all  of the good and evil of humanity is  signed nattara versus marijuana is one  of my favorite battles that has ever  occurred in all of media in regards to  ant under specifically though it took a  huge step up by giving us a glimpse of  the pinnacle of power in the series and  one that I'm not sure we'll ever be  equaled and I think that the 2011 anime  did a marvelous job in bringing it to  life as for other primary figures are  the world god I think serve is more of  an antagonistic purpose in this arc the  marijuana does in retrospect I actually  seen marijuana as his own protagonist  working through life as best he could  consistently learning and adjusting his  instincts but the Royal Guard were a  different story altogether although most  of them do go through a similar sort of  journey the  that comes to mind immediately would of  course be you P who learns to master and  apply his rage to better serve the King  but who also comes to an understanding  with humanity at least briefly and I  guess specifically in the case of NACO  but that sort of thing was still really  great to see because you P had the  potential to be just a big dumb strong  guy but in the end he's probably at the  Royal Guard that I respect the most  with that said Peter was the one who  interested me most though especially  because they were specialists and they  came equipped with some cool abilities  and an adorable design from the very  moment they were shown with kites  severed head and while Peter was  obviously never close to the power of  that of marijuana Vito always came  equipped with the feeling that they  would use their abilities in a far more  sinister way and just stuff like the  Warped artistic depiction of them  whenever a character was thinking about  Peter made them such a uniquely scary  presence which is a fine thing to  achieve with such a cutesy design the  ultimate credit I have Peter though is  that I