ieve that  this was a pretty big mistake for the  anime to have made especially when  Gaughan's entire car  Dirac is centered around his emotional  attachment kite to pull that off  you need an entire series of development  there is another situation though which  comes in the form of gyro now this is  something that confused the hell out of  me when I was watching the anime because  out of absolutely nowhere we've got this  incredibly detailed flashback of a  character who we never see and not only  that but also learning that the story  never pays off  I mean well finanical Kodu mentioned  Shiro at the end but I went on to assume  that gyro was the human who became  marijuana and that was that and I think  that the anime did quite deliberately  lead viewers to this conclusion which  was why it was an incredible shock to me  to find out that not only is gyro a  completely separate character converted  into an ant but in the manga he was  actually seen and Takashi made a very  big deal about he and gon having an  eventual meeting potentially setting up  a true ultimate form of evil in the  series and I get why the anime did it  because even in the manga this whole  Shiro situation is not paid off so why  not wrap a neat little bow around it  right here but it has led to a great  misunderstanding within the Honda Honda  community concerning gyro which is  something that I find myself constantly  battling with however within the context  of the anime as a product of its own  look it works I guess however knowing  how things are on the manga I really do  wish that they would have stuck to the  original events but to begin to  summarize my thoughts I both love and  hate this arc it has the highest of  highs and the lowest of lows in the  series everything that happens from the  palace invasion onwards I consider to be  some of the greatest storytelling ever  implemented but getting to that point is  such a difficult task and there are just  far too many random fights against  insignificant ants that blow to this arc  into oblivion I cannot even imagine what  it would have been like to spend 8 years  of my life following the series during  these events however I can't deny that  all of the effort put into it does turn  out to be more than worth it despite all  of the fatigue I felt when going through  this arc it reached a point of becoming  one of the most compelling and special  pieces of media that I've ever consumed  and it's a huge contributing factor to  why I decided to heavily feature hunt  hunter on this channel so I will always  remember it incredibly fondly and I feel  like most of the people who were able to  survive this are very much in the same  boat so well done Takashi for telling  this great long form story and  completely redefining hunter hunter in  the process and that pretty much does it  for this review of the Chimera ant op if  you enjoyed this video and the content  this channel produced in general and  please do consider donating to the new  world review patreon because the support  of all of your amazing people is what  continues to make this channel possible  and to pay  Tron isn't quite your style please do  leave this video a like share or  subscribe because it also helps for this  channel and incredible amount and if  you'd like to join the fun at anytime  then please do head over to my desk  world server where a wide array of  January takes place on a daily basis and  finally please do comment with your  thoughts on the Chimera ant Ark this has  been the new world review and I'll see  you next time  [Music]

